 game with a  single-player campaign perhaps the most  intriguing title of the spring though is  Tacoma brought to you by the same minds  who created the surprise yet gone home  Tacoma takes the game's investigative  mystery feel and moves it to the  claustrophobic interior of a derelict  Space Station where something has  definitely gone wrong players have to  try and uncover the mystery of what  happened to the crew honestly it's so  creepy already we're not sure we even  want to know summer and fall  considering the gaming industry is full  of delays and outright cancellations  it's no wonder Studios a hesitant to  give their games firm release dates too  far in advance but while we don't know  for sure when these games are going to  come out here are some of the other  titles you should be able to play  sometime in 2017 inspired by old Mickey  Mouse cartoons  cuphead has captured the imagination of  retro gamers and side scroller fans  everywhere rumor has it the designers  are putting the final touches on co-op  mode so no further delays are  anticipated besides cuphead there are a  handful of other new intellectual  properties to keep an eye on this year  scalebound is an epic third-person  action game where you get to control a  freakin dragon which is always cool  [Music]  from down  days go on features more apocalyptic  survival fare only this time in one of  our nation's national parks so that's  you know it's nice and Detroit become  human fights back against urban decline  with a futuristic neo-noir story about  androids every choice has major  ramifications for the storyline  if sequels are more your thing though  don't worry because 2017 has a metric  ton of returning franchises starting  with God of War yes  Kratos is back in the story which sees  the older and more grizzled warrior  taking on a new challenge osteoporosis  I'm fallen and I can't get up no no just  kidding  he's fighting in the Norse gods and  monsters this time there are plenty of  other fan favorite franchises making a  comeback in 2017 Shenmue 3 makes its  long-awaited return after getting crowd  funded on Kickstarter Legend of Zelda  breath of the wild takes the Nintendo  classic and adds a dash of modern  gameplay Dead Island 2 moves the zombie  survival game to Los Angeles and spoke  is's on slapstick multiplayer gameplay  quake champions is the latest  first-person shooter arena showdown  agents of mayhem is the saints row 3rd  person shooter spin-off revolving around  an anti-terrorist organization crackdown  3 features an open-world sandbox and the  ability to level civilizations with  godlike powers then there's also a  Spider Man game coming from the  developers of ratchet &amp; clank which will  no doubt somehow tie into the release of  the summer film blockbuster spider-man  homecoming and then there's Super Mario  switch a game so secret we don't even  know the actual title yet but wait  that's not all two of the biggest  releases of the year are also seagulls  South Park the fractured but whole  builds on the surprisingly great RPG  elements of South Park the stick of  truth  2  liver and even broader and more detailed  world this time parroting the superhero  genre and the mere announcement that  there would be a Red Dead Redemption -  was enough to rocket the game to the top  of everyone's wish list for next  Christmas here's hoping Santa has a huge  sleigh because he's going to need it to  carry all these great games thanks for  watching click the loop icon to  subscribe to our youtube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  you love to  [Music]
 

